      "properties": {},
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Video upscale (SeedVR2 7B)\n\nThe order is: generate, watch it, like it, then come here.\n\n**Measured:** 608x352 at 39 frames became 1864x1080 in 3.5 minutes, audio\npasses through untouched. 124 frames take about 11 minutes.\n\n**Why not ESRGAN.** It pulls every frame on its own and never sees the\nneighbours, so video comes out flickering, worst on faces and fine texture.\nSeedVR2 was trained on video and keeps frames consistent.\n\n## Do not break these\n\n**batch_size = 5.** The model takes 15.4 GB, which leaves under eight gigabytes\nof a single card for activations. A batch of 13, and certainly 41, dies with\nOOM at 1080p. Five is also the minimum at which frames start informing each\nother. The value has to be of the form 4n+1: 5, 9, 13.\n\n**blocks_to_swap = 0.** Swapping blocks to CPU looks like the cure for OOM, but\nhere it hangs the process for good: the GPU drops to zero and the job will not\neven cancel on interrupt. Only a restart clears it. Leave it off.\n\n**The upscaler runs on one card.** The node does not spread weights across\ndevices, so it hits the 24 GB of cuda:0 rather than the combined pool. That is\nwhere the small batch comes from.\n\n## If you need something else\n\n- bigger batch: drop `resolution` to 720;\n- or switch to the 3B model, half the size, less detail;\n- 4K on 7B will not fit under these constraints.\n\n**The second weight set** `seedvr2_ema_7b_sharp_fp16` cuts harder. Skin usually\nlooks better on the regular one, tech and textures on sharp.\n\n**Do not download anything heavy in parallel.** The page cache fills up, the\nkernel goes off to compact memory, and loading the model onto the card stalls\nfor five minutes with the GPU at zero. It looks exactly like a hung job.\n"
      ]
    }
